%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 182c9b1add361454880f8d772a4f0e3c, type: 3}
  m_Name: Hub3 Bearing
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  steps:
  - titlePhrase: 
    descriptionPhrase: Hub3_Description_1
    audioPhrase: Hub3_Audio_1
    animationStateName: 1
    fallbackTitle: 
    fallbackDescription: Start to learn how to align and assemble the Hub3 bearing
      step by step.
  - titlePhrase: 
    descriptionPhrase: Hub3_Description_2
    audioPhrase: Hub3_Audio_2
    animationStateName: 2
    fallbackTitle: 
    fallbackDescription: First, take the inner ring and place it properly on the
      assembly surface. Insert and tighten the bolt into the inner ring at this stage
      to provide proper support and prevent movement during assembly. Confirm that
      the inner ring is stable and correctly aligned.
  - titlePhrase: 
    descriptionPhrase: Hub3_Description_3
    audioPhrase: Hub3_Audio_3
    animationStateName: 3
    fallbackTitle: 
    fallbackDescription: Next, position the  row of balls with the cages and make
      sure the balls are evenly spaced and properly seated inside the groove. Adjust
      the cage if necessary to achieve proper alignment before proceeding.
  - titlePhrase: 
    descriptionPhrase: Hub3_Description_4
    audioPhrase: Hub3_Audio_4
    animationStateName: 4
    fallbackTitle: 
    fallbackDescription: After that, carefully place the  ball cage assembly on the
      opposite side of the inner ring and align both rows correctly with their respective
      raceway grooves. Ensure there is no tilting or uneven placement.
  - titlePhrase: 
    descriptionPhrase: Hub3_Description_5
    audioPhrase: Hub3_Audio_5
    animationStateName: 5
    fallbackTitle: 
    fallbackDescription: Next, take Seal S1 and attach it carefully on the inner
      ring side where the first ball cage assembly is positioned to ensure proper
      grip and secure seating. Make sure the seal is evenly aligned and properly
      seated without twisting.
  - titlePhrase: 
    descriptionPhrase: Hub3_Description_6
    audioPhrase: Hub3_Audio_6
    animationStateName: 6
    fallbackTitle: 
    fallbackDescription: Now, take the B1 ring set and gently align it inner Ring,
      ensuring proper positioning without disturbing the ball arrangement. Make sure
      the raceways match correctly before applying pressure.
  - titlePhrase: 
    descriptionPhrase: Hub3_Description_7
    audioPhrase: Hub3_Audio_7
    animationStateName: 7
    fallbackTitle: 
    fallbackDescription: Press the outer ring slowly and evenly using a press machine
      until it is fully seated and properly aligned with the inner ring assembly.
      Avoid sudden or uneven force to prevent misalignment.
  - titlePhrase: 
    descriptionPhrase: Hub3_Description_8
    audioPhrase: Hub3_Audio_8
    animationStateName: 8
    fallbackTitle: 
    fallbackDescription: Then, install the seal rings on the end side carefully to
      protect the internal components and lock the bearing assembly. Ensure the seals
      are evenly seated and not twisted.
